{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-83761","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-116286","text":"Runefort Protocol — v0.1"}]},{"id":"blk-83762","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116287","marks":["bold"],"text":"A layout protocol for living, file-backed, tile-grid web apps."}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83764","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116288","marks":["bold"],"text":"Part of the [&] Protocol stack"},{"id":"spn-116289","text":" · "},{"id":"spn-116290","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/ECOSYSTEM.md"}],"text":"Ecosystem overview"},{"id":"spn-116291","text":" · "},{"id":"spn-116292","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/PULSE/docs/THREE_PROTOCOL_STACK.md"}],"text":"Three-protocol stack"},{"id":"spn-116293","text":" · "},{"id":"spn-116294","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/STACK_COMPLETION.md"}],"text":"Stack status"}]}],"id":"blk-83763","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-83765","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116295","text":"Status: draft v0.1 Owner: runefort.com Date: 2026-04-25 Position: protocol-level. Independent of [&], PULSE, PRISM. May be used by them; does not require them."}]},{"id":"blk-83766","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116296","marks":["bold"],"text":"Related documents:"}]},{"id":"blk-83767","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83769","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116297","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/docs/spec/runefort.core.md"}],"text":"@runefort/core — Reference Web Component Framework v0.1"}]}],"id":"blk-83768","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83771","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116298","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/docs/spec/runefort.dsl.md"}],"text":".rune DSL — v0.1"}]}],"id":"blk-83770","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83773","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116299","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/.claude/prompts/RFORT-BUILD-ORDER.md"}],"text":"Interactive Layer — Build Order"}]}],"id":"blk-83772","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83775","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116300","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/.claude/prompts/RFORT-1_BYOK.md"}],"text":"RFort-1 — BYOK Modal + OpenRouter Key Storage"}]}],"id":"blk-83774","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83777","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116301","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/.claude/prompts/RFORT-2_MCP.md"}],"text":"RFort-2 — MCP Proxy + Client + Connection Panel"}]}],"id":"blk-83776","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83779","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116302","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/.claude/prompts/RFORT-3_CHAT.md"}],"text":"RFort-3 — Chat Panel with Fort-Aware Navigation"}]}],"id":"blk-83778","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83781","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116303","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/.claude/prompts/RFORT-4_TOKENFLOWS.md"}],"text":"RFort-4 — Token Flow Animations on Edges"}]}],"id":"blk-83780","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83783","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116304","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/.claude/prompts/RFORT-5_REPO_IMPORT.md"}],"text":"RFort-5 — Repo Import → Fort Generator"}]}],"id":"blk-83782","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83785","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116305","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/.claude/prompts/RFORT-6_WORKSPACES.md"}],"text":"RFort-6 — Workspace Switcher + Supabase Persistence"}]}],"id":"blk-83784","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-83786","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-116306","text":"0. What this is, in one paragraph"}]},{"id":"blk-83787","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116307","text":"Runefort is a small declarative protocol for describing a "},{"id":"spn-116308","marks":["bold"],"text":"tiled, file-backed UI layout"},{"id":"spn-116309","text":". You declare "},{"id":"spn-116310","marks":["italic"],"text":"rooms"},{"id":"spn-116311","text":" (tiles), "},{"id":"spn-116312","marks":["italic"],"text":"claims"},{"id":"spn-116313","text":" (file-system regions each room owns), "},{"id":"spn-116314","marks":["italic"],"text":"neighbors"},{"id":"spn-116315","text":" (adjacency for navigation), and "},{"id":"spn-116316","marks":["italic"],"text":"state bindings"},{"id":"spn-116317","text":" (how live state colors a tile). A conformant renderer compiles the declaration to a CSS grid, surfaces each claim's content for inline viewing or editing, and overlays live state. The protocol is the contract between the declaration and the renderer. Nothing more."}]},{"id":"blk-83788","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116318","text":"It is not a workforce platform. It is not a supervisor framework. It is not a graph visualization library. It is the "},{"id":"spn-116319","marks":["bold"],"text":"layout language"},{"id":"spn-116320","text":" that those things can be built with."}]},{"id":"blk-83789","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-116321","text":"1. Why a protocol (not a library)"}]},{"id":"blk-83790","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83792","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116322","marks":["bold"],"text":"Renderer-portable."},{"id":"spn-116323","text":" The same "},{"id":"spn-116324","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.json"},{"id":"spn-116325","text":" should render in Elixir/Phoenix, TypeScript/React, or static HTML. The protocol is the only thing they share."}]}],"id":"blk-83791","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83794","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116326","marks":["bold"],"text":"Diffable."},{"id":"spn-116327","text":" Layouts live in version control as text. Reviews become readable. SVG graph layouts cannot do this."}]}],"id":"blk-83793","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83796","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116328","marks":["bold"],"text":"Extensible by composition."},{"id":"spn-116329","text":" Apps add "},{"id":"spn-116330","marks":["italic"],"text":"vocabularies"},{"id":"spn-116331","text":" (e.g. "},{"id":"spn-116332","marks":["code"],"text":"supervisor"},{"id":"spn-116333","text":", "},{"id":"spn-116334","marks":["code"],"text":"dashboard"},{"id":"spn-116335","text":", "},{"id":"spn-116336","marks":["code"],"text":"wiki-page"},{"id":"spn-116337","text":") on top of the core primitives. The protocol does not know about supervisors."}]}],"id":"blk-83795","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83798","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116338","marks":["bold"],"text":"No runtime layout engine required."},{"id":"spn-116339","text":" All layout is compile-time deterministic. No d3, no dagre, no jitter."}]}],"id":"blk-83797","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-83799","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-116340","text":"2. Core primitives"}]},{"id":"blk-83800","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116341","text":"Four primitives. That is the entire vocabulary."}]},{"id":"blk-83801","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-116342","text":"2.1 Room"}]},{"id":"blk-83802","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116343","text":"A room is a tile in the grid. It has an id, a position, a size, and arbitrary metadata."}]},{"id":"blk-83803","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"id\": \"memory\",\n  \"position\": [0, 0],\n  \"size\": [3, 2],\n  \"label\": \"memory.ex\",\n  \"meta\": {}\n}"},{"id":"blk-83804","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116344","marks":["code"],"text":"position"},{"id":"spn-116345","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-116346","marks":["code"],"text":"size"},{"id":"spn-116347","text":" are integer cell coordinates in a CSS grid. "},{"id":"spn-116348","marks":["code"],"text":"[0,0]"},{"id":"spn-116349","text":" is top-left. "},{"id":"spn-116350","marks":["code"],"text":"size: [3,2]"},{"id":"spn-116351","text":" means 3 columns wide, 2 rows tall. The renderer is free to choose the cell pixel size; the protocol only specifies cell counts."}]},{"id":"blk-83805","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-116352","text":"2.2 Claim"}]},{"id":"blk-83806","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116353","text":"A claim is a file-system region a room \"owns.\" A renderer uses claims to (a) list which files belong to a room and (b) surface those files inline — either as a viewer or an editor — when the user activates the room. Optional behaviors include generating external-editor handoff URLs ("},{"id":"spn-116354","marks":["code"],"text":"vscode://"},{"id":"spn-116355","text":", "},{"id":"spn-116356","marks":["code"],"text":"cursor://"},{"id":"spn-116357","text":", "},{"id":"spn-116358","marks":["code"],"text":"zed://"},{"id":"spn-116359","text":") for users who prefer their own tools."}]},{"id":"blk-83807","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"room\": \"memory\",\n  \"pattern\": \"lib/my_app/memory/**/*.ex\",\n  \"anchor\": \"lib/my_app/forge/memory.ex#L24\"\n}"},{"id":"blk-83808","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116360","marks":["code"],"text":"pattern"},{"id":"spn-116361","text":" is a glob. "},{"id":"spn-116362","marks":["code"],"text":"anchor"},{"id":"spn-116363","text":" is the canonical file the room represents (the one a click on the tile opens)."}]},{"id":"blk-83809","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-116364","text":"2.3 Neighbor"}]},{"id":"blk-83810","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116365","text":"A neighbor declares an adjacency between two rooms. Neighbors drive keyboard navigation ("},{"id":"spn-116366","marks":["code"],"text":"h/j/k/l"},{"id":"spn-116367","text":"), focus order, and may be rendered as connecting lines."}]},{"id":"blk-83811","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{ \"from\": \"memory\", \"to\": \"deploy\", \"kind\": \"adjacent\" }"},{"id":"blk-83812","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116368","marks":["code"],"text":"kind"},{"id":"spn-116369","text":" is one of: "},{"id":"spn-116370","marks":["code"],"text":"adjacent"},{"id":"spn-116371","text":" (touching), "},{"id":"spn-116372","marks":["code"],"text":"linked"},{"id":"spn-116373","text":" (logical link, may not be touching), "},{"id":"spn-116374","marks":["code"],"text":"nested"},{"id":"spn-116375","text":" (one contains the other)."}]},{"id":"blk-83813","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-116376","text":"2.4 State binding"}]},{"id":"blk-83814","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116377","text":"A state binding tells the renderer how to color a room based on a runtime signal. The protocol defines the "},{"id":"spn-116378","marks":["italic"],"text":"binding"},{"id":"spn-116379","text":", not the signal source — signals are pushed to the renderer over whatever transport the host app provides (WebSocket, SSE, polling, static)."}]},{"id":"blk-83815","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"room\": \"memory\",\n  \"signal\": \"kappa\",\n  \"thresholds\": [\n    { \"if\": \"< 0.3\", \"class\": \"cold\" },\n    { \"if\": \"< 0.6\", \"class\": \"warm\" },\n    { \"if\": \">= 0.6\", \"class\": \"hot\" }\n  ]\n}"},{"id":"blk-83816","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116380","marks":["code"],"text":"class"},{"id":"spn-116381","text":" is a token the renderer maps to CSS. The protocol reserves five canonical classes: "},{"id":"spn-116382","marks":["code"],"text":"cold"},{"id":"spn-116383","text":", "},{"id":"spn-116384","marks":["code"],"text":"warm"},{"id":"spn-116385","text":", "},{"id":"spn-116386","marks":["code"],"text":"hot"},{"id":"spn-116387","text":", "},{"id":"spn-116388","marks":["code"],"text":"fault"},{"id":"spn-116389","text":", "},{"id":"spn-116390","marks":["code"],"text":"idle"},{"id":"spn-116391","text":". Apps may add custom classes — renderers should ignore unknown classes gracefully (treat as "},{"id":"spn-116392","marks":["code"],"text":"cold"},{"id":"spn-116393","text":")."}]},{"id":"blk-83817","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-116394","text":"3. Document shape"}]},{"id":"blk-83818","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116395","text":"A complete "},{"id":"spn-116396","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.json"},{"id":"spn-116397","text":" is just an object containing arrays of the four primitives, plus header metadata."}]},{"id":"blk-83819","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"runefort\": \"0.1\",\n  \"title\": \"my_app forge floor\",\n  \"grid\": { \"columns\": 6, \"rows\": 4 },\n  \"rooms\": [ ... ],\n  \"claims\": [ ... ],\n  \"neighbors\": [ ... ],\n  \"state_bindings\": [ ... ],\n  \"vocabulary\": \"core\"\n}"},{"id":"blk-83820","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116398","marks":["code"],"text":"grid.columns"},{"id":"spn-116399","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-116400","marks":["code"],"text":"grid.rows"},{"id":"spn-116401","text":" are the total grid dimensions. "},{"id":"spn-116402","marks":["code"],"text":"vocabulary"},{"id":"spn-116403","text":" is the name of the extension vocabulary in use; "},{"id":"spn-116404","marks":["code"],"text":"\"core\""},{"id":"spn-116405","text":" means no extensions."}]},{"id":"blk-83821","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-116406","text":"4. The DSL surface (host-language sugar)"}]},{"id":"blk-83822","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116407","text":"Hosts may expose a DSL that compiles to the JSON above. The DSL is "},{"id":"spn-116408","marks":["bold"],"text":"not normative"},{"id":"spn-116409","text":" — only the JSON is. A reference Elixir DSL:"}]},{"id":"blk-83823","kind":"code","language":"elixir","text":"defmodule MyApp.Floor do\n  use Runefort.Layout, columns: 6, rows: 4\n\n  room :memory,\n    at: {0, 0}, size: {3, 2},\n    claims: ~r{lib/my_app/memory/},\n    anchor: \"lib/my_app/forge/memory.ex:24\"\n\n  room :deploy,\n    at: {3, 0}, size: {3, 2},\n    claims: ~r{lib/my_app/deploy/}\n\n  neighbors :memory => :deploy\n\n  bind :memory, signal: :kappa,\n    cold: \"< 0.3\", warm: \"< 0.6\", hot: \">= 0.6\"\nend"},{"id":"blk-83824","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116410","text":"A reference TypeScript DSL:"}]},{"id":"blk-83825","kind":"code","language":"ts","text":"const floor = layout({ columns: 6, rows: 4 }, [\n  room(\"memory\", { at: [0,0], size: [3,2], claims: \"lib/my_app/memory/**\" }),\n  room(\"deploy\", { at: [3,0], size: [3,2], claims: \"lib/my_app/deploy/**\" }),\n  neighbor(\"memory\", \"deploy\"),\n  bind(\"memory\", \"kappa\", { cold: \"< 0.3\", warm: \"< 0.6\", hot: \">= 0.6\" }),\n]);"},{"id":"blk-83826","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116411","text":"Both compile to the same JSON. Either is conformant. Neither is privileged."}]},{"id":"blk-83827","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-116412","text":"5. Renderer contract"}]},{"id":"blk-83828","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116413","text":"A conformant renderer MUST:"}]},{"id":"blk-83829","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83831","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116414","marks":["bold"],"text":"Layout."},{"id":"spn-116415","text":" Render rooms in a CSS grid (or visually equivalent) using each room's "},{"id":"spn-116416","marks":["code"],"text":"position"},{"id":"spn-116417","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-116418","marks":["code"],"text":"size"},{"id":"spn-116419","text":". The grid MUST be deterministic — given the same JSON, the rendered DOM order MUST be stable."}]}],"id":"blk-83830","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83833","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116420","marks":["bold"],"text":"Anchors."},{"id":"spn-116421","text":" Resolve each room's "},{"id":"spn-116422","marks":["code"],"text":"anchor"},{"id":"spn-116423","text":" to its content (the file or content region the room represents). Activating a tile MUST surface that content — by default, inline within the host page (viewer or editor). Renderers MAY additionally offer an external-editor handoff URL as a secondary action, but inline surfacing is the canonical behavior."}]}],"id":"blk-83832","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83835","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116424","marks":["bold"],"text":"State classes."},{"id":"spn-116425","text":" Apply CSS classes from "},{"id":"spn-116426","marks":["code"],"text":"state_bindings"},{"id":"spn-116427","text":" to each room's root element. Class names MUST be predictable: "},{"id":"spn-116428","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort-state-cold"},{"id":"spn-116429","text":", "},{"id":"spn-116430","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort-state-hot"},{"id":"spn-116431","text":", etc."}]}],"id":"blk-83834","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83837","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116432","marks":["bold"],"text":"Accessibility."},{"id":"spn-116433","text":" Each room MUST be focusable (keyboard) and have a stable accessible name (the room's "},{"id":"spn-116434","marks":["code"],"text":"label"},{"id":"spn-116435","text":" or "},{"id":"spn-116436","marks":["code"],"text":"id"},{"id":"spn-116437","text":")."}]}],"id":"blk-83836","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83839","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116438","marks":["bold"],"text":"Neighbor navigation."},{"id":"spn-116439","text":" Arrow keys (or "},{"id":"spn-116440","marks":["code"],"text":"h/j/k/l"},{"id":"spn-116441","text":") MUST move focus along "},{"id":"spn-116442","marks":["code"],"text":"neighbor"},{"id":"spn-116443","text":" edges. Renderers MAY also expose mouse navigation; keyboard support is required."}]}],"id":"blk-83838","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-83840","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116444","text":"A conformant renderer SHOULD:"}]},{"id":"blk-83841","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83843","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116445","text":"Provide an inline editor (not just a read-only viewer) for the focused room's "},{"id":"spn-116446","marks":["code"],"text":"anchor"},{"id":"spn-116447","text":" when the host environment supports text editing."}]}],"id":"blk-83842","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83845","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116448","text":"Highlight neighbor adjacencies on hover/focus."}]}],"id":"blk-83844","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83847","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116449","text":"Re-render on signal change without full reload."}]}],"id":"blk-83846","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-83848","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116450","text":"A conformant renderer MAY:"}]},{"id":"blk-83849","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83851","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116451","text":"Add domain-specific vocabularies (see §6)."}]}],"id":"blk-83850","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83853","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116452","text":"Display additional metadata from "},{"id":"spn-116453","marks":["code"],"text":"meta"},{"id":"spn-116454","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-83852","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83855","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116455","text":"Animate state class transitions."}]}],"id":"blk-83854","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83857","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116456","text":"Offer external-editor handoff URLs ("},{"id":"spn-116457","marks":["code"],"text":"vscode://"},{"id":"spn-116458","text":", "},{"id":"spn-116459","marks":["code"],"text":"cursor://"},{"id":"spn-116460","text":", "},{"id":"spn-116461","marks":["code"],"text":"zed://"},{"id":"spn-116462","text":") as a secondary action for users who prefer their own tools. Renderers that run outside the browser (e.g. static-site generators, server-rendered HTML with no JS) MAY treat handoff as their primary surfacing strategy and still claim conformance."}]}],"id":"blk-83856","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-83858","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-116463","text":"6. Vocabularies (extension points)"}]},{"id":"blk-83859","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116464","text":"The protocol's core knows nothing about supervisors, dashboards, or wikis. Apps declare a "},{"id":"spn-116465","marks":["italic"],"text":"vocabulary"},{"id":"spn-116466","text":" — a named bundle of extra fields on "},{"id":"spn-116467","marks":["code"],"text":"meta"},{"id":"spn-116468","text":", extra signals, and extra state classes."}]},{"id":"blk-83860","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"runefort\": \"0.1\",\n  \"vocabulary\": \"supervisor-floor.v1\",\n  \"rooms\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"memory\",\n      \"position\": [0,0], \"size\": [3,2],\n      \"meta\": {\n        \"supervisor\": {\n          \"autonomy\": \"advise\",\n          \"uptime_seconds\": 957840,\n          \"last_action\": \"consolidated 47 nodes\"\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}"},{"id":"blk-83861","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116469","text":"The "},{"id":"spn-116470","marks":["code"],"text":"supervisor-floor.v1"},{"id":"spn-116471","text":" vocabulary defines what "},{"id":"spn-116472","marks":["code"],"text":"meta.supervisor"},{"id":"spn-116473","text":" contains. A renderer that doesn't know "},{"id":"spn-116474","marks":["code"],"text":"supervisor-floor.v1"},{"id":"spn-116475","text":" MUST still render the layout correctly — it just won't display the supervisor-specific overlay. "},{"id":"spn-116476","marks":["bold"],"text":"Vocabulary unknown = degrade, don't fail."}]},{"id":"blk-83862","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116477","text":"Reserved vocabularies (managed by the protocol authors):"}]},{"id":"blk-83863","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83865","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116478","marks":["code"],"text":"core"},{"id":"spn-116479","text":" — the four primitives, no extensions."}]}],"id":"blk-83864","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83867","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116480","marks":["code"],"text":"supervisor-floor.v1"},{"id":"spn-116481","text":" — for [&]/Runefort supervisor workforce apps."}]}],"id":"blk-83866","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83869","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116482","marks":["code"],"text":"codebase-atlas.v1"},{"id":"spn-116483","text":" — for repository visualization apps."}]}],"id":"blk-83868","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83871","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116484","marks":["code"],"text":"dashboard-grid.v1"},{"id":"spn-116485","text":" — for metric/observability tile dashboards."}]}],"id":"blk-83870","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-83872","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116486","text":"Custom vocabularies are namespaced freely ("},{"id":"spn-116487","marks":["code"],"text":"com.example.my-vocab.v1"},{"id":"spn-116488","text":"). The protocol does not require registration."}]},{"id":"blk-83873","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-116489","text":"7. Non-goals"}]},{"id":"blk-83874","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116490","text":"Explicit, so the protocol stays small:"}]},{"id":"blk-83875","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83877","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116491","marks":["bold"],"text":"Not a graph visualization protocol."},{"id":"spn-116492","text":" Force-directed layouts, dagre, hierarchies — out of scope. Runefort is grids only. If you need a graph, use a graph tool."}]}],"id":"blk-83876","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83879","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116493","marks":["bold"],"text":"Not a state-management protocol."},{"id":"spn-116494","text":" How signals are computed, where they live, how they're transported — host's problem."}]}],"id":"blk-83878","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83881","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116495","marks":["bold"],"text":"Not a workforce / supervision framework."},{"id":"spn-116496","text":" That's a "},{"id":"spn-116497","marks":["italic"],"text":"vocabulary"},{"id":"spn-116498","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-116499","marks":["code"],"text":"supervisor-floor.v1"},{"id":"spn-116500","text":"), built on top."}]}],"id":"blk-83880","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83883","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116501","marks":["bold"],"text":"Not a presentation framework."},{"id":"spn-116502","text":" No theming spec, no animation spec. CSS is the renderer's job."}]}],"id":"blk-83882","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83885","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116503","marks":["bold"],"text":"Not coupled to [&], PULSE, or PRISM."},{"id":"spn-116504","text":" A "},{"id":"spn-116505","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.json"},{"id":"spn-116506","text":" describing a recipe app is fully conformant."}]}],"id":"blk-83884","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-83886","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-116507","text":"8. Versioning"}]},{"id":"blk-83887","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116508","text":"Semver for the protocol itself. The top-level "},{"id":"spn-116509","marks":["code"],"text":"\"runefort\": \"0.1\""},{"id":"spn-116510","text":" field is the protocol version, NOT the renderer version."}]},{"id":"blk-83888","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83890","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116511","marks":["bold"],"text":"Major bump"},{"id":"spn-116512","text":" = breaking JSON shape change."}]}],"id":"blk-83889","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83892","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116513","marks":["bold"],"text":"Minor bump"},{"id":"spn-116514","text":" = additive (new optional fields, new reserved vocabularies, new state classes)."}]}],"id":"blk-83891","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83894","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116515","marks":["bold"],"text":"Patch"},{"id":"spn-116516","text":" = clarification only, no behavior change."}]}],"id":"blk-83893","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-83895","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116517","text":"A renderer MUST refuse documents with a major version it does not support. A renderer SHOULD render documents with a higher minor version, ignoring fields it does not recognize."}]},{"id":"blk-83896","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-116518","text":"9. Reference framework — "},{"id":"spn-116519","marks":["code"],"text":"@runefort/core"}]},{"id":"blk-83897","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116520","text":"The canonical browser-side reference implementation is "},{"id":"spn-116521","marks":["bold"],"text":"`@runefort/core`"},{"id":"spn-116522","text":": a small set of Web Components ("},{"id":"spn-116523","marks":["code"],"text":"<rune-floor>"},{"id":"spn-116524","text":", "},{"id":"spn-116525","marks":["code"],"text":"<rune-room>"},{"id":"spn-116526","text":", "},{"id":"spn-116527","marks":["code"],"text":"<rune-claim>"},{"id":"spn-116528","text":", "},{"id":"spn-116529","marks":["code"],"text":"<rune-link>"},{"id":"spn-116530","text":") implementing this protocol with no framework dependency. ~5KB minified target. Specified in "},{"id":"spn-116531","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.core.md"},{"id":"spn-116532","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-83898","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116533","text":"Why a reference framework, not just a renderer:"}]},{"id":"blk-83899","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83901","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116534","marks":["bold"],"text":"Zero-build adoption."},{"id":"spn-116535","text":" Drop one "},{"id":"spn-116536","marks":["code"],"text":"<script type=\"module\">"},{"id":"spn-116537","text":" tag into any HTML page and the protocol is rendered. No bundler, no npm, no framework."}]}],"id":"blk-83900","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83903","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116538","marks":["bold"],"text":"Universal embedding."},{"id":"spn-116539","text":" Custom Elements work inside React, Vue, Svelte, Solid, Lit, Astro, Phoenix LiveView, Rails view templates, plain HTML. The framework adapters are ~1KB each, not full reimplementations."}]}],"id":"blk-83902","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83905","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116540","marks":["bold"],"text":"Single reactivity story."},{"id":"spn-116541","text":" Property setters on "},{"id":"spn-116542","marks":["code"],"text":"<rune-floor>"},{"id":"spn-116543","text":" push signal updates; rooms recompute their state class. No virtual DOM, no opinionated state library — composes with whatever the host app already uses."}]}],"id":"blk-83904","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-83906","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116544","text":"Conformant alternatives may exist. "},{"id":"spn-116545","marks":["code"],"text":"@runefort/core"},{"id":"spn-116546","text":" is the reference, not the only option. A pure-Phoenix-LiveView renderer or a server-rendered static-HTML emitter are both valid conformant implementations."}]},{"id":"blk-83907","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-116547","text":"9.1 Authoring surfaces"}]},{"id":"blk-83908","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116548","text":"The same protocol is reachable through three authoring surfaces, all equivalent and all round-trippable:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-83910","spans":[{"id":"spn-116549","text":"Surface"}]},{"id":"blk-83911","spans":[{"id":"spn-116550","text":"Format"}]},{"id":"blk-83912","spans":[{"id":"spn-116551","text":"Use case"}]}],"id":"blk-83909","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-83913","spans":[{"id":"spn-116552","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.json"}]},{"id":"blk-83914","spans":[{"id":"spn-116553","text":"JSON"}]},{"id":"blk-83915","spans":[{"id":"spn-116554","text":"Programmatic generation, tooling integration, canonical persistence"}]}],[{"id":"blk-83916","spans":[{"id":"spn-116555","marks":["code"],"text":"<rune-*>"},{"id":"spn-116556","text":" HTML"}]},{"id":"blk-83917","spans":[{"id":"spn-116557","text":"Custom Elements"}]},{"id":"blk-83918","spans":[{"id":"spn-116558","text":"Hand-written pages, embedding inside existing apps"}]}],[{"id":"blk-83919","spans":[{"id":"spn-116559","marks":["code"],"text":".rune"},{"id":"spn-116560","text":" DSL"}]},{"id":"blk-83920","spans":[{"id":"spn-116561","text":"Curly-brace declarative"}]},{"id":"blk-83921","spans":[{"id":"spn-116562","text":"Hand-authored layouts, version control reviewability"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-83922","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116563","text":"The DSL is specified in "},{"id":"spn-116564","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.dsl.md"},{"id":"spn-116565","text":". The CLI converts losslessly between all three."}]},{"id":"blk-83923","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-116566","text":"9.2 Planned tree"}]},{"id":"blk-83924","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"runefort/\n  spec/\n    runefort.protocol.md       ← this document\n    runefort.core.md           ← @runefort/core web component spec\n    runefort.dsl.md            ← .rune DSL spec\n    schema.json                ← JSON schema for runefort.json\n  packages/\n    core/                      ← @runefort/core (web components, target ≤5KB)\n    cli/                       ← runefort CLI (compile/fmt/to-rune)\n    react/                     ← @runefort/react adapter (~1KB)\n    vue/                       ← @runefort/vue adapter\n    svelte/                    ← @runefort/svelte adapter\n    liveview/                  ← @runefort/liveview adapter\n  examples/\n    no-framework/              ← raw HTML, proves \"runs anywhere\"\n    supervisor-floor/          ← the [&] use case, proves supervisor-floor.v1\n    codebase-atlas/            ← non-[&], proves genericity\n    dashboard-grid/            ← non-[&], proves genericity"},{"id":"blk-83925","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116567","text":"Two non-[&] examples are required before we cut v0.1 final. Otherwise we're an [&] dashboard with a spec attached."}]},{"id":"blk-83926","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-116568","text":"9.3 Build order (v0.1)"}]},{"id":"blk-83927","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83929","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116569","marks":["code"],"text":"@runefort/core"},{"id":"spn-116570","text":" — the four web components + "},{"id":"spn-116571","marks":["code"],"text":"mount(json)"},{"id":"spn-116572","text":". Smallest meaningful artifact."}]}],"id":"blk-83928","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83931","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116573","text":"Playground at runefort.com — live "},{"id":"spn-116574","marks":["code"],"text":".rune"},{"id":"spn-116575","text":" editor → rendered floor. The shareable demo."}]}],"id":"blk-83930","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83933","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116576","text":"CLI compile path — "},{"id":"spn-116577","marks":["code"],"text":".rune"},{"id":"spn-116578","text":" → "},{"id":"spn-116579","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.json"},{"id":"spn-116580","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-116581","marks":["code"],"text":".rune"},{"id":"spn-116582","text":" → static HTML."}]}],"id":"blk-83932","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83935","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116583","text":"Adapters — React, then LiveView, then others as demand appears."}]}],"id":"blk-83934","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-83936","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116584","text":"Adapters wait until non-zero users exist. Shipping all adapters before having users is the wrong direction of optimization."}]},{"id":"blk-83937","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-116585","text":"10. Relationship to the [&] stack"}]},{"id":"blk-83938","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116586","text":"Runefort is "},{"id":"spn-116587","marks":["bold"],"text":"independent of"},{"id":"spn-116588","text":" [&]. It does not import, depend on, or require any [&] protocol. However:"}]},{"id":"blk-83939","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83941","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116589","marks":["code"],"text":"[&]"},{"id":"spn-116590","text":" capability descriptors MAY be embedded in "},{"id":"spn-116591","marks":["code"],"text":"meta"},{"id":"spn-116592","text":" under "},{"id":"spn-116593","marks":["code"],"text":"supervisor-floor.v1"},{"id":"spn-116594","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-83940","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83943","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116595","text":"PULSE manifest phases MAY drive room generation in tooling that bridges PULSE → Runefort."}]}],"id":"blk-83942","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83945","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116596","text":"PRISM scores MAY be a signal source for state bindings."}]}],"id":"blk-83944","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-83946","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116597","text":"These are "},{"id":"spn-116598","marks":["italic"],"text":"integration patterns"},{"id":"spn-116599","text":", not protocol requirements. A Runefort layout that knows nothing about [&] is fully conformant."}]},{"id":"blk-83947","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-116600","text":"11. Open questions for v0.2"}]},{"id":"blk-83948","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83950","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116601","marks":["bold"],"text":"Nesting."},{"id":"spn-116602","text":" A room inside a room (zoomable). Worth adding to core, or push to a vocabulary?"}]}],"id":"blk-83949","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83952","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116603","marks":["bold"],"text":"Streaming layout edits."},{"id":"spn-116604","text":" Today the JSON is whole-document. Should there be a patch format?"}]}],"id":"blk-83951","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83954","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116605","marks":["bold"],"text":"Manifest discovery."},{"id":"spn-116606","text":" Does a renderer auto-discover "},{"id":"spn-116607","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.json"},{"id":"spn-116608","text":" in a repo, or is the path always provided?"}]}],"id":"blk-83953","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83956","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116609","marks":["bold"],"text":"Multiple anchors per room."},{"id":"spn-116610","text":" Today one anchor. Real codebases have N files per logical region."}]}],"id":"blk-83955","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-83957","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116611","text":"These are explicitly deferred. v0.1 ships with the four primitives and nothing else."}]},{"id":"blk-83958","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116612","marks":["italic"],"text":"This spec is the contract. Everything in `runefort.com/docs/spec/README.md` (the spatial-cognition / dark-factory spec) is now reframed as the `supervisor-floor.v1` vocabulary plus the `runefort.dark_factory` reference application — both built on top of this protocol."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaieragzrtil3odmuzeizsqrmcrauayl5kgyaahl4mpl7arlnxnxly5eya","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}